{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkzXG1jzXAhmC64LabpVbF","type":"tool_result","content":"3630\t    },\n3631\t    {\n3632\t      \"id\": \"US-162\",\n3633\t      \"title\": \"Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\",\n3634\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n3635\t      \"description\": \"React 19.2 introduces cacheSignal() for Server Components, providing an AbortSignal that fires when the cache() entry's lifetime ends. This allows in-flight fetch requests to be aborted when the cached result will no longer be used (e.g., when cache is invalidated mid-request). For server-side data fetching (room availability, pricing from external APIs), cacheSignal ensures abandoned fetches don't hold open connections unnecessarily.\",\n3636\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3637\t        \"At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal() to pass an abort signal\",\n3638\t        \"Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\",\n3639\t        \"No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (requires React 19.2 types from Next.js 16)\",\n3640\t        \"Server Component rendering is not regressed (same data fetched correctly)\"\n3641\t      ],\n3642\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3643\t        \"cacheSignal() is Server Components only — not usable in Client Components or Route Handlers\",\n3644\t        \"Pattern: const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))\",\n3645\t        \"React 19.2 feature, available with Next.js 16\",\n3646\t        \"Source: https://react.dev/reference/react/cache#caching-with-a-signal\"\n3647\t      ],\n3648\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3649\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n3650\t      \"passes\": false,\n3651\t      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n3652\t      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T01:42:45Z\"\n3653\t    },\n3654\t    {\n3655\t      \"id\": \"US-163\",\n3656\t      \"title\": \"Implement Google Tag Manager with Consent Mode v2\",\n3657\t      \"priority\": \"high\",\n3658\t      \"description\": \"Install GTM with Consent Mode v2 so all six consent parameters (ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, personalization_storage) are correctly signalled before any Google tags fire. Required since March 2024 for Google Ads conversion tracking to function with EU/international visitors. Enables the marketing team to manage tags without code deploys.\",\n3659\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3660\t        \"GTM container script loaded in layout.tsx using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager component\",\n3661\t        \"Consent Mode v2 default state is set to 'denied' before GTM loads via a gtag.js dataLayer push in a beforeInteractive script\",\n3662\t        \"All six consent parameters are initialised: ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, security_storage\",\n3663\t        \"Consent state is updated to 'granted' upon PDPA cookie consent banner acceptance\",\n3664\t        \"GTM Consent Overview in GTM UI shows all tags are consent-aware\",\n3665\t        \"Verified in Google Tag Assistant that no Google tags fire before consent is granted\"\n3666\t      ],\n3667\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3668\t        \"Load GTM using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager with lazyOnload strategy\",\n3669\t        \"Initialise default consent state in a <Script strategy='beforeInteractive'> block\",\n3670\t        \"gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ... }) must execute before GTM container\",\n3671\t        \"Update consent on banner accept: gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ... })\",\n3672\t        \"Reference: https://developers.google.com/tag-platform/security/guides/consent\"\n3673\t      ],\n3674\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3675\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n3676\t      \"passes\": true\n3677\t    },\n3678\t    {\n3679\t      \"id\": \"US-164\",\n3680\t      \"title\": \"Implement Facebook Conversions API (CAPI) for server-side event tracking\",\n3681\t      \"priority\": \"high\",\n3682\t      \"description\": \"Add a Next.js Route Handler that sends key booking-intent events (PageView, ViewContent on room pages, Contact on form submission) directly to the Meta Conversions API server-side. Server-side tracking bypasses browser ad blockers and iOS 14+ restrictions, significantly improving Facebook/Instagram Ads attribution accuracy for retargeting campaigns targeting international backpackers.\",\n3683\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3684\t        \"POST /api/meta-events Route Handler implemented and sends events to Meta Conversions API v21.0\",\n3685\t        \"Events tracked: PageView, ViewContent (room page), Contact (inquiry form submit)\",\n3686\t        \"Each event has a unique event_id that matches the corresponding browser-side Pixel event for deduplication\",\n3687\t        \"User data fields (email, phone) are SHA-256 hashed before transmission per Meta requirements\",\n3688\t        \"FACEBOOK_PIXEL_ID and FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN stored as Vercel environment variables\",\n3689\t        \"Meta Events Manager Test Events Tool confirms events arrive and deduplicate correctly\"\n3690\t      ],\n3691\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3692\t        \"Use Meta Marketing API v21.0 endpoint: POST https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/{pixel-id}/events\",\n3693\t        \"Required payload: data[].event_name, data[].event_time (Unix timestamp), data[].event_source_url, data[].action_source='website'\",\n3694\t        \"Hash user data: crypto.createHash('sha256').update(email.trim().toLowerCase()).digest('hex')\",\n3695\t        \"Browser-side Pixel is still needed alongside CAPI — use the same event_id for deduplication\",\n3696\t        \"Reference: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/marketing-api/conversions-api/\"\n3697\t      ],\n3698\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3699\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n3700\t      \"passes\": true\n3701\t    },\n3702\t    {\n3703\t      \"id\": \"US-165\",\n3704\t      \"title\": \"WCAG 2.1 SC 2.1.1 – Keyboard: ensure all functionality is keyboard operable\",\n3705\t      \"priority\": \"high\",\n3706\t      \"description\": \"Audit all interactive functionality to ensure it can be operated entirely via keyboard without requiring specific timing. Custom components using div/span (image gallery carousel, mobile drawer nav, room tabs) must receive tabindex, role, and keyboard event handlers. This is WCAG 2.1 Level A — failing this makes the site completely unusable for keyboard-only users including many people with motor disabilities.\",\n3707\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3708\t        \"All navigation menus, dropdowns, and mobile drawer can be opened/closed using Enter, Space, and Escape keys\",\n3709\t        \"Gallery carousel supports Left/Right Arrow key navigation between images\",\n3710\t        \"Room type tabs on /rooms support Arrow Left/Right key navigation per ARIA tab pattern\",\n3711\t        \"Any custom <div role='button'> or interactive span elements handle keydown Enter and Space events\",\n3712\t        \"WCAG 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap satisfied: pressing Escape or Shift+Tab can always exit any modal or overlay\",\n3713\t        \"Full keyboard navigation path tested manually with Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, and Arrow keys\"\n3714\t      ],\n3715\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3716\t        \"Non-native interactive elements need: tabindex='0', appropriate ARIA role, onKeyDown handler for Enter/Space\",\n3717\t        \"Modals must implement focus trap: keep Tab/Shift+Tab within the modal, restore focus to trigger element on close\",\n3718\t        \"Use @radix-ui/react primitives (included in shadcn/ui) — they have keyboard interaction built-in per ARIA APG\",\n3719\t        \"ARIA keyboard patterns reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/\",\n3720\t        \"Reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/keyboard.html\"\n3721\t      ],\n3722\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3723\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n3724\t      \"passes\": true\n3725\t    },\n3726\t    {\n3727\t      \"id\": \"US-166\",\n3728\t      \"title\": \"Add axe-core automated accessibility testing in CI/CD pipeline\",\n3729\t      \"priority\": \"high\",\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a16f91ac-2e27-4e8a-bf46-dfd84cbb51f9","uuid":"fc916e7e-5695-407e-a234-8ea6544801d8","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:43:41.728Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\prd.json","content":"    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-162\",\n      \"title\": \"Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"React 19.2 introduces cacheSignal() for Server Components, providing an AbortSignal that fires when the cache() entry's lifetime ends. This allows in-flight fetch requests to be aborted when the cached result will no longer be used (e.g., when cache is invalidated mid-request). For server-side data fetching (room availability, pricing from external APIs), cacheSignal ensures abandoned fetches don't hold open connections unnecessarily.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal() to pass an abort signal\",\n        \"Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\",\n        \"No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (requires React 19.2 types from Next.js 16)\",\n        \"Server Component rendering is not regressed (same data fetched correctly)\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"cacheSignal() is Server Components only — not usable in Client Components or Route Handlers\",\n        \"Pattern: const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))\",\n        \"React 19.2 feature, available with Next.js 16\",\n        \"Source: https://react.dev/reference/react/cache#caching-with-a-signal\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T01:42:45Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-163\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Google Tag Manager with Consent Mode v2\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"description\": \"Install GTM with Consent Mode v2 so all six consent parameters (ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, personalization_storage) are correctly signalled before any Google tags fire. Required since March 2024 for Google Ads conversion tracking to function with EU/international visitors. Enables the marketing team to manage tags without code deploys.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GTM container script loaded in layout.tsx using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager component\",\n        \"Consent Mode v2 default state is set to 'denied' before GTM loads via a gtag.js dataLayer push in a beforeInteractive script\",\n        \"All six consent parameters are initialised: ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, security_storage\",\n        \"Consent state is updated to 'granted' upon PDPA cookie consent banner acceptance\",\n        \"GTM Consent Overview in GTM UI shows all tags are consent-aware\",\n        \"Verified in Google Tag Assistant that no Google tags fire before consent is granted\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Load GTM using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager with lazyOnload strategy\",\n        \"Initialise default consent state in a <Script strategy='beforeInteractive'> block\",\n        \"gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ... }) must execute before GTM container\",\n        \"Update consent on banner accept: gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ... })\",\n        \"Reference: https://developers.google.com/tag-platform/security/guides/consent\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-164\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Facebook Conversions API (CAPI) for server-side event tracking\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a Next.js Route Handler that sends key booking-intent events (PageView, ViewContent on room pages, Contact on form submission) directly to the Meta Conversions API server-side. Server-side tracking bypasses browser ad blockers and iOS 14+ restrictions, significantly improving Facebook/Instagram Ads attribution accuracy for retargeting campaigns targeting international backpackers.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"POST /api/meta-events Route Handler implemented and sends events to Meta Conversions API v21.0\",\n        \"Events tracked: PageView, ViewContent (room page), Contact (inquiry form submit)\",\n        \"Each event has a unique event_id that matches the corresponding browser-side Pixel event for deduplication\",\n        \"User data fields (email, phone) are SHA-256 hashed before transmission per Meta requirements\",\n        \"FACEBOOK_PIXEL_ID and FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN stored as Vercel environment variables\",\n        \"Meta Events Manager Test Events Tool confirms events arrive and deduplicate correctly\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Use Meta Marketing API v21.0 endpoint: POST https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/{pixel-id}/events\",\n        \"Required payload: data[].event_name, data[].event_time (Unix timestamp), data[].event_source_url, data[].action_source='website'\",\n        \"Hash user data: crypto.createHash('sha256').update(email.trim().toLowerCase()).digest('hex')\",\n        \"Browser-side Pixel is still needed alongside CAPI — use the same event_id for deduplication\",\n        \"Reference: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/marketing-api/conversions-api/\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-165\",\n      \"title\": \"WCAG 2.1 SC 2.1.1 – Keyboard: ensure all functionality is keyboard operable\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"description\": \"Audit all interactive functionality to ensure it can be operated entirely via keyboard without requiring specific timing. Custom components using div/span (image gallery carousel, mobile drawer nav, room tabs) must receive tabindex, role, and keyboard event handlers. This is WCAG 2.1 Level A — failing this makes the site completely unusable for keyboard-only users including many people with motor disabilities.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"All navigation menus, dropdowns, and mobile drawer can be opened/closed using Enter, Space, and Escape keys\",\n        \"Gallery carousel supports Left/Right Arrow key navigation between images\",\n        \"Room type tabs on /rooms support Arrow Left/Right key navigation per ARIA tab pattern\",\n        \"Any custom <div role='button'> or interactive span elements handle keydown Enter and Space events\",\n        \"WCAG 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap satisfied: pressing Escape or Shift+Tab can always exit any modal or overlay\",\n        \"Full keyboard navigation path tested manually with Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, and Arrow keys\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Non-native interactive elements need: tabindex='0', appropriate ARIA role, onKeyDown handler for Enter/Space\",\n        \"Modals must implement focus trap: keep Tab/Shift+Tab within the modal, restore focus to trigger element on close\",\n        \"Use @radix-ui/react primitives (included in shadcn/ui) — they have keyboard interaction built-in per ARIA APG\",\n        \"ARIA keyboard patterns reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/\",\n        \"Reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/keyboard.html\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-166\",\n      \"title\": \"Add axe-core automated accessibility testing in CI/CD pipeline\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",","numLines":100,"startLine":3630,"totalLines":6092}}}
