{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019uRQ5R4DFNawQSL33i89ae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { createHmac } from \"crypto\";\n2\timport { CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG } from \"@/config/channel-manager\";\n3\timport type { ChannelManagerAvailability, ChannelManagerBooking } from \"./channel-manager-types\";\n4\t\n5\texport class Beds24Client {\n6\t  private apiKey: string;\n7\t  private propertyId: string;\n8\t  private baseUrl: string;\n9\t\n10\t  constructor() {\n11\t    this.apiKey = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.apiKey;\n12\t    this.propertyId = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.propertyId;\n13\t    this.baseUrl = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.apiBaseUrl;\n14\t  }\n15\t\n16\t  async getAvailability(\n17\t    checkin: string,\n18\t    checkout: string,\n19\t  ): Promise<ChannelManagerAvailability[]> {\n20\t    if (!this.isConfigured()) {\n21\t      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n22\t    }\n23\t\n24\t    try {\n25\t      const params = new URLSearchParams({\n26\t        apiKey: this.apiKey,\n27\t        propid: this.propertyId,\n28\t        checkin,\n29\t        checkout,\n30\t      });\n31\t\n32\t      const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/getAvailability?${params}`, {\n33\t        cache: \"no-store\",\n34\t      });\n35\t\n36\t      if (!response.ok) {\n37\t        console.error(\"Beds24 API error:\", response.statusText);\n38\t        return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n39\t      }\n40\t\n41\t      const data = await response.json();\n42\t      return this.parseAvailabilityResponse(data, checkin, checkout);\n43\t    } catch (error) {\n44\t      console.error(\"Beds24 fetch failed:\", error);\n45\t      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n46\t    }\n47\t  }\n48\t\n49\t  private parseAvailabilityResponse(\n50\t    data: unknown,\n51\t    checkin: string,\n52\t    checkout: string,\n53\t  ): ChannelManagerAvailability[] {\n54\t    // Beds24 API returns an object with 'roomtypes' key containing array of room availability\n55\t    if (!data || typeof data !== \"object\" || !(\"roomtypes\" in data)) {\n56\t      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n57\t    }\n58\t\n59\t    const roomData = data as Record<string, unknown>;\n60\t    const roomtypes = roomData.roomtypes;\n61\t\n62\t    if (!Array.isArray(roomtypes)) {\n63\t      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n64\t    }\n65\t\n66\t    return roomtypes\n67\t      .map((room: unknown) => {\n68\t        if (typeof room !== \"object\" || !room) return null;\n69\t        const r = room as Record<string, unknown>;\n70\t\n71\t        // Extract data from Beds24 response structure\n72\t        const roomId = String(r.id || r.roomId || \"\");\n73\t        const roomName = String(r.name || r.roomName || \"\");\n74\t        const available = Number(r.available || 0);\n75\t        const total = Number(r.totalInventory || r.total || 0);\n76\t        const rate = Number(r.rate || 0);\n77\t\n78\t        return {\n79\t          roomId,\n80\t          roomName,\n81\t          checkin,\n82\t          checkout,\n83\t          available,\n84\t          total,\n85\t          rate,\n86\t          currency: \"MYR\",\n87\t        };\n88\t      })\n89\t      .filter((r): r is ChannelManagerAvailability => r !== null && r.roomId !== \"\");\n90\t  }\n91\t\n92\t  async syncBooking(booking: Partial<ChannelManagerBooking>): Promise<boolean> {\n93\t    if (!this.isConfigured()) return false;\n94\t\n95\t    try {\n96\t      const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/putBooking`, {\n97\t        method: \"POST\",\n98\t        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n99\t        body: JSON.stringify({\n100\t          apiKey: this.apiKey,\n101\t          propid: this.propertyId,\n102\t          guestName: booking.guestName,\n103\t          guestEmail: booking.guestEmail,\n104\t          guestPhone: booking.guestPhone,\n105\t          checkin: booking.checkin,\n106\t          checkout: booking.checkout,\n107\t          roomId: booking.roomId,\n108\t          noOfGuests: booking.adults || 1,\n109\t          status: \"confirmed\",\n110\t        }),\n111\t      });\n112\t\n113\t      return response.ok;\n114\t    } catch (error) {\n115\t      console.error(\"Booking sync failed:\", error);\n116\t      return false;\n117\t    }\n118\t  }\n119\t\n120\t  validateWebhook(payload: string, signature: string | null): boolean {\n121\t    if (!signature) return false;\n122\t    const hmac = createHmac(\"sha256\", CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.webhook.secret);\n123\t    hmac.update(payload);\n124\t    return hmac.digest(\"hex\") === signature;\n125\t  }\n126\t\n127\t  private isConfigured(): boolean {\n128\t    return this.apiKey !== \"\" && this.propertyId !== \"\";\n129\t  }\n130\t\n131\t  private placeholderAvailability(\n132\t    checkin: string,\n133\t    checkout: string,\n134\t  ): ChannelManagerAvailability[] {\n135\t    const nights = Math.ceil(\n136\t      (new Date(checkout).getTime() - new Date(checkin).getTime()) /\n137\t        (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n138\t    );\n139\t\n140\t    return [\n141\t      {\n142\t        roomId: \"standard-capsule\",\n143\t        roomName: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n144\t        checkin,\n145\t        checkout,\n146\t        available: 18,\n147\t        total: 18,\n148\t        rate: 35 * nights,\n149\t        currency: \"MYR\",\n150\t      },\n151\t      {\n152\t        roomId: \"premium-capsule\",\n153\t        roomName: \"Premium Capsule Pod\",\n154\t        checkin,\n155\t        checkout,\n156\t        available: 6,\n157\t        total: 6,\n158\t        rate: 45 * nights,\n159\t        currency: \"MYR\",\n160\t      },\n161\t    ];\n162\t  }\n163\t}\n164\t\n165\texport const beds24Client = new Beds24Client();\n166\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a16f91ac-2e27-4e8a-bf46-dfd84cbb51f9","uuid":"2a6b9181-cc80-430d-85ee-2c6b512294a6","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:45:13.489Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\lib\\beds24-client.ts","content":"import { createHmac } from \"crypto\";\nimport { CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG } from \"@/config/channel-manager\";\nimport type { ChannelManagerAvailability, ChannelManagerBooking } from \"./channel-manager-types\";\n\nexport class Beds24Client {\n  private apiKey: string;\n  private propertyId: string;\n  private baseUrl: string;\n\n  constructor() {\n    this.apiKey = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.apiKey;\n    this.propertyId = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.propertyId;\n    this.baseUrl = CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.beds24.apiBaseUrl;\n  }\n\n  async getAvailability(\n    checkin: string,\n    checkout: string,\n  ): Promise<ChannelManagerAvailability[]> {\n    if (!this.isConfigured()) {\n      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n\n    try {\n      const params = new URLSearchParams({\n        apiKey: this.apiKey,\n        propid: this.propertyId,\n        checkin,\n        checkout,\n      });\n\n      const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/getAvailability?${params}`, {\n        cache: \"no-store\",\n      });\n\n      if (!response.ok) {\n        console.error(\"Beds24 API error:\", response.statusText);\n        return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n      }\n\n      const data = await response.json();\n      return this.parseAvailabilityResponse(data, checkin, checkout);\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(\"Beds24 fetch failed:\", error);\n      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n  }\n\n  private parseAvailabilityResponse(\n    data: unknown,\n    checkin: string,\n    checkout: string,\n  ): ChannelManagerAvailability[] {\n    // Beds24 API returns an object with 'roomtypes' key containing array of room availability\n    if (!data || typeof data !== \"object\" || !(\"roomtypes\" in data)) {\n      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n\n    const roomData = data as Record<string, unknown>;\n    const roomtypes = roomData.roomtypes;\n\n    if (!Array.isArray(roomtypes)) {\n      return this.placeholderAvailability(checkin, checkout);\n    }\n\n    return roomtypes\n      .map((room: unknown) => {\n        if (typeof room !== \"object\" || !room) return null;\n        const r = room as Record<string, unknown>;\n\n        // Extract data from Beds24 response structure\n        const roomId = String(r.id || r.roomId || \"\");\n        const roomName = String(r.name || r.roomName || \"\");\n        const available = Number(r.available || 0);\n        const total = Number(r.totalInventory || r.total || 0);\n        const rate = Number(r.rate || 0);\n\n        return {\n          roomId,\n          roomName,\n          checkin,\n          checkout,\n          available,\n          total,\n          rate,\n          currency: \"MYR\",\n        };\n      })\n      .filter((r): r is ChannelManagerAvailability => r !== null && r.roomId !== \"\");\n  }\n\n  async syncBooking(booking: Partial<ChannelManagerBooking>): Promise<boolean> {\n    if (!this.isConfigured()) return false;\n\n    try {\n      const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/putBooking`, {\n        method: \"POST\",\n        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n          apiKey: this.apiKey,\n          propid: this.propertyId,\n          guestName: booking.guestName,\n          guestEmail: booking.guestEmail,\n          guestPhone: booking.guestPhone,\n          checkin: booking.checkin,\n          checkout: booking.checkout,\n          roomId: booking.roomId,\n          noOfGuests: booking.adults || 1,\n          status: \"confirmed\",\n        }),\n      });\n\n      return response.ok;\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(\"Booking sync failed:\", error);\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n\n  validateWebhook(payload: string, signature: string | null): boolean {\n    if (!signature) return false;\n    const hmac = createHmac(\"sha256\", CHANNEL_MANAGER_CONFIG.webhook.secret);\n    hmac.update(payload);\n    return hmac.digest(\"hex\") === signature;\n  }\n\n  private isConfigured(): boolean {\n    return this.apiKey !== \"\" && this.propertyId !== \"\";\n  }\n\n  private placeholderAvailability(\n    checkin: string,\n    checkout: string,\n  ): ChannelManagerAvailability[] {\n    const nights = Math.ceil(\n      (new Date(checkout).getTime() - new Date(checkin).getTime()) /\n        (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n    );\n\n    return [\n      {\n        roomId: \"standard-capsule\",\n        roomName: \"Standard Capsule Pod\",\n        checkin,\n        checkout,\n        available: 18,\n        total: 18,\n        rate: 35 * nights,\n        currency: \"MYR\",\n      },\n      {\n        roomId: \"premium-capsule\",\n        roomName: \"Premium Capsule Pod\",\n        checkin,\n        checkout,\n        available: 6,\n        total: 6,\n        rate: 45 * nights,\n        currency: \"MYR\",\n      },\n    ];\n  }\n}\n\nexport const beds24Client = new Beds24Client();\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EzVFE97z9Xnx5VZ1HMm8G3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I found it. The `beds24-client.ts` has:\n1. Line 32: `fetch()` call in `getAvailability()` \n2. Line 96: `fetch()` call in `syncBooking()`\n\nThese are the perfect candidates for implementing `cacheSignal()`. Since these are called from the Route Handler in `api/ari/route.ts` which is a Server Component context (Route Handlers are basically server-side), I can wrap the fetch calls with `cache()` and use `cacheSignal()`.\n\nAccording to the story, I need to:\n1. Use `cache()` to wrap external fetch functions\n2. Use `cacheSignal()` to pass an abort signal to fetch requests\n3. The abort signal should fire when the cache entry's lifetime ends\n\nLet me now understand the structure better and plan the implementation.\n\nThe pattern should be:\n```typescript\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\n\nconst getCachedAvailability = cache(async (checkin: string, checkout: string) => {\n  const params = new URLSearchParams({\n    apiKey: this.apiKey,\n    propid: this.propertyId,\n    checkin,\n    checkout,\n  });\n\n  const response = await fetch(`${this.baseUrl}/getAvailability?${params}`, {\n    signal: cacheSignal(),\n  });\n  // ... rest of the code\n});\n```\n\nActually, wait. Looking at the code structure, `beds24Client` is a class. The `getAvailability` method is an instance method, not a top-level function. In React's `cache()` pattern, we need to cache at the function level, not at the method level.\n\nI think the best approach would be to:\n1. Import `cache` from \"react\" \n2. Create a cached wrapper function around the fetch call\n3. Use `cacheSignal()` in the fetch options\n\n\n4. `cacheSignal()` is available within the `cache()` context, so I can use it directly in the cached function. The pattern from React docs shows: `const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: 